## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CKNE-to-quotas mapping, token-based fairness, and SLA guarantees in a real-world multi-tenant dispatch scenario.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-quotas mapping
- Token-bucket with a global minute cap
- Minute-by-minute reallocation and carryover
- SLA baseline with priority to high-CKNE tenants

## Code Example
```javascript
function allocateQuotas(totalCap, tenants) {
  const sumCKNE = tenants.reduce((s,t)=>s+t.ckne,0) || 1;
  return tenants.map(t => {
    const q = Math.floor(totalCap * (t.ckne / sumCKNE));
    return {tenant: t.tenant, quota: Math.max(1, q)};
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle new tenants joining or CKNE updates during a minute?
- What telemetry would you collect to verify fairness and SLA adherence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CKNE-aware tracing in serverless multi-tenant workflows with per-tenant sampling. Emphasizes deterministic sampling, fault isolation, and fidelity under bursts.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health propagation across hops
- per-tenant sampling policies
- deterministic sampling using traceId hashing
- serverless orchestration and edge aggregation
- fidelity during micro-bursts

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldSample(tenantId, traceId, health, rates) {
  const rate = rates[tenantId] ?? 0;
  const seed = hashCode(traceId + '|' + tenantId);
  return (Math.abs(seed) % 1000) < rate * 1000;
}
function hashCode(s){
  let h=0; for(let i=0;i<s.length;i++){ h=(h*31 + s.charCodeAt(i))|0; } return h;
}
```

